          "text": "You’re right that your repo has `semantic-release: \"25.0.1\"` in `package.json`, but that **is not what’s running in CI right now**, and the `ENONPMTOKEN` error is coming from the npm plugin, not from OIDC.\n\n### 1. Where the versions actually come from\n\n- The log says:\n\n  > `[semantic-release] › ℹ  Running semantic-release version 24.2.9`\n\n  That version string is coming from **the action’s own install**, not from your devDependency.\n\n- In `release.yml` you have:\n\n```yaml\n- name: 🚀 Semantic Release\n  id: semrel\n  uses: cycjimmy/semantic-release-action@v5\n  env:\n    GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n```\n\n- Per the action’s README for `@v6` (same idea for `@v5`):\n\n  > “If no version range is specified… then semantic-release version 24.x is used.”\n\nSo:\n\n- **semantic-release core** version is controlled by the action (`@v5` right now),  \n- Your `devDependencies` entry (`\"semantic-release\": \"25.0.1\"`) is only used if you run `npx semantic-release` yourself, not when using the action.\n\n### 2. Why you’re seeing `ENONPMTOKEN`\n\nFrom the `@semantic-release/npm` README you pasted:\n\n> `verifyConditions` — Verify the presence of the `NPM_TOKEN` environment variable, or an `.npmrc` file, and verify the authentication method is valid.\n\nAnd your error stack is exactly from that plugin:\n\n> `SemanticReleaseError: No npm token specified.`  \n> at `@semantic-release/npm/lib/set-npmrc-auth.js`\n\nSo, regardless of OIDC / trusted publishing:\n\n- The **plugin itself** currently refuses to run `verifyConditions` without `NPM_TOKEN` (or a pre‑auth `.npmrc`), and that’s what’s failing.\n\n### 3. What this means for you\n\nWith your current setup (semantic-release via `cycjimmy/semantic-release-action` + `@semantic-release/npm`):\n\n- There is **no fully tokenless path** supported today; the plugin expects `NPM_TOKEN`.\n- The trusted‑publishing docs you quoted are about **how npm authenticates once called**, but `@semantic-release/npm` still insists on seeing a token up front.\n\nSo you have two realistic options:\n\n- **Use an npm automation token (recommended to get unblocked):**\n\n  ```yaml\n  - name: 🚀 Semantic Release\n    id: semrel\n    uses: cycjimmy/semantic-release-action@v5   # or @v6\n    env:\n      GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n      NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n  ```\n\n  where `NPM_TOKEN` is a scoped **automation** token for `@growthspace-engineering` (not a broad PAT, and rotateable).\n\n- **Or drop `@semantic-release/npm` and own `npm publish` yourself** (what we briefly tried with `@semantic-release/exec`), in which case we’re back to debugging npm’s OIDC behavior directly.\n\nGiven the time you’ve already sunk into OIDC and that the blocker is now clearly the plugin’s hard `NPM_TOKEN` check, the practical way forward is to create a narrowly scoped `NPM_TOKEN` and wire it in as above.",
