          "text": "Short answer: **no, neither of those will remove the `NPM_TOKEN` requirement with your current setup.**\n\n### Why `@v6` of the action won’t help\n\n- `cycjimmy/semantic-release-action@v6` just:\n  - Installs a semantic‑release version (24.x by default, or what you pass via `semantic_version`),\n  - Then runs `semantic-release`.\n- Your error is coming from **`@semantic-release/npm`’s own `verifyConditions` step**:\n\n  > `SemanticReleaseError: No npm token specified.`\n\n  That plugin, including the current 13.x you already have in `devDependencies`, still explicitly checks for `NPM_TOKEN` (or an `.npmrc`) and throws `ENONPMTOKEN` if neither is present.\n\nSwitching the action from `@v5` to `@v6` doesn’t change that plugin behavior; it will still call the same `@semantic-release/npm`, which will still demand `NPM_TOKEN`.\n\n### Why pinning `semantic_version` also doesn’t fix it\n\n- You can do:\n\n  ```yaml\n  uses: cycjimmy/semantic-release-action@v6\n  with:\n    semantic_version: 25.0.1\n  ```\n\n- That upgrades **semantic‑release core**, but your `package.json` already pins `@semantic-release/npm` at `13.1.1`, and that is what semantic‑release will load.\n- The `ENONPMTOKEN` check lives in `@semantic-release/npm`, not in the core version. So even with core 25.x, the plugin will still fail `verifyConditions` without `NPM_TOKEN`.\n\n### Net: what actually changes the situation\n\nYou effectively have three levers:\n\n1. **Provide `NPM_TOKEN`** (automation token, scoped, rotated) and keep using `@semantic-release/npm` → quickest path to green.\n2. **Stop using `@semantic-release/npm` for npmjs** (remove it from `.releaserc.json`) and own the `npm publish` yourself via `@semantic-release/exec` + trusted publishing → more work, we already saw it’s finicky.\n3. **Wait for / contribute a change to `@semantic-release/npm`** that truly treats trusted publishing as tokenless and then upgrade to that plugin version.\n\nGiven the current plugin behavior, upgrading the action or pinning `semantic_version` alone will not eliminate the `NPM_TOKEN` requirement.",
